---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contribute"
  description="Share your story of learning or teaching Bharatanatyam."
>
  <!-- Leaflet CSS — served from CDN, bypasses /_astro/ bundling -->
  <link
    slot="head"
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.min.css"
    crossorigin="anonymous"
    referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
  />

  <h1>Contribute to the Living Archive</h1>

  <p>Bharatanatyam is passed down through people, and no single collection can
  document every teacher, lineage, or experience. This project is an ongoing
  effort to record some of that knowledge and make it available for others
  to study.</p>

  <p>If you learn, teach, perform, or research Bharatanatyam, you can help
  expand the living archive.</p>

  <h2>Ways to contribute</h2>

  <dl class="contrib-ways">
    <dt>Share an oral history</dt>
    <dd>Record or write about a lesson you remember, a teacher who shaped your
    practice, or something you hope future dancers will carry forward.</dd>

    <dt>Add context or a correction</dt>
    <dd>If you notice an error, have an alternative interpretation, or can
    provide useful context for an existing entry, your contribution can help
    make the archive more accurate.</dd>

    <dt>Contribute a śloka recording</dt>
    <dd>Recordings from other teachers or lineages can help document differences
    in pronunciation and recitation that the current corpus does not
    represent.</dd>

    <dt>Share a translation or explanation</dt>
    <dd>Translations and contextual notes in Tamil, Hindi, or other languages
    can help make the material accessible to a wider community.</dd>
  </dl>

  <hr />

  <h2>How to contribute</h2>

  <p>Use the form below to describe your contribution and provide the relevant
  audio or text. You may request to be credited by name or to contribute
  anonymously.</p>

  <div class="gform-embed">
    <iframe
      src="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeomEehO81eJLiBIu3BxZibTOX72F-Fwz67BjUZLHTz0YKnzA/viewform?embedded=true"
      width="640"
      height="1450"
      frameborder="0"
      marginheight="0"
      marginwidth="0"
    >Loading…</iframe>
  </div>

  <hr />

  <h2>Where contributors are from</h2>

  <div
    id="contributor-map"
    class="contrib-map"
    data-regions={JSON.stringify(contributorRegions)}
  ></div>

  <p class="map-note">Locations are approximate and represent regions, not addresses.</p>

  <hr />

  <h2>A note on consent</h2>

  <p>Submissions will be reviewed before being added to the public archive.
  The form explains how material may be used, whether it may be published or
  adapted, and how contributors can ask questions or request withdrawal. No
  contribution will be published without the appropriate consent.</p>

  <!-- Leaflet JS + map & form init — loaded after body so L is available -->
  <script
    slot="tail"
    is:inline
    src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.min.js"
    crossorigin="anonymous"
    referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
  ></script>

  <script slot="tail" is:inline>
    // ── Map ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    const mapEl = document.getElementById('contributor-map');
    if (mapEl && typeof L !== 'undefined') {
      const regions = JSON.parse(mapEl.dataset.regions || '[]');

      const map = L.map('contributor-map', {
        scrollWheelZoom: false,
        zoomControl: true,
      });

      L.tileLayer('https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', {
        attribution:
          '&copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors',
        maxZoom: 19,
      }).addTo(map);

      const markers = regions.map(function(r) {
        const m = L.circleMarker([r.lat, r.lng], {
          radius: 4,
          fillColor: '#b5531a',
          color: '#b5531a',
          weight: 0,
          fillOpacity: 0.75,
        }).addTo(map);
        m.bindPopup('<strong>' + r.label + '</strong>');
        return m;
      });

      if (markers.length) {
        const group = L.featureGroup(markers);
        map.fitBounds(group.getBounds().pad(0.35));
      } else {
        map.setView([20, 0], 2);
      }
    }

  </script>

</BaseLayout>
